WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.268
The dashboard is a high-value system because it concentrates security data and may control integrations.

00:00:06.268 --> 00:00:09.146
Protect it with individual accounts, strong passwords,

00:00:09.146 --> 00:00:11.202
and multi-factor authentication where available.

00:00:11.202 --> 00:00:14.492
Remove default credentials and avoid shared administrator accounts.

00:00:14.492 --> 00:00:17.781
Patch the operating system, dashboard software, databases, libraries,

00:00:17.781 --> 00:00:20.659
and supporting services through a managed process.

00:00:20.659 --> 00:00:25.182
Test significant updates, back up configuration, and retain a rollback path.

00:00:25.182 --> 00:00:30.117
Unsupported components create long-term risk even when the interface appears to work.

00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:35.873
Place the dashboard on an appropriate network segment and restrict inbound and outbound communication.

00:00:35.873 --> 00:00:38.340
Collectors should reach only required services.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.863
Administrative interfaces should not be exposed directly to the public internet.

00:00:42.863 --> 00:00:45.331
Use a controlled VPN, authenticated gateway,

00:00:45.331 --> 00:00:48.620
or similarly protected method for legitimate remote access.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.498
Store API keys, database passwords, signing keys,

00:00:51.498 --> 00:00:56.844
and service credentials in protected secret storage rather than source files, browser code,

00:00:56.844 --> 00:00:58.077
or shared notes.

00:00:58.077 --> 00:01:01.778
Give each integration narrow permissions, rotate credentials when needed,

00:01:01.778 --> 00:01:05.067
and revoke them when a service is retired.

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:08.357
Use encrypted connections where appropriate and validate certificates.

00:01:08.357 --> 00:01:11.646
Apply secure session settings, rate limits, input validation,

00:01:11.646 --> 00:01:14.114
and defenses supplied by maintained frameworks.

00:01:14.114 --> 00:01:19.048
Backups and exported reports deserve the same protection as the live dashboard

00:01:19.048 --> 00:01:21.926
because they may contain equivalent sensitive data.

00:01:21.926 --> 00:01:25.216
Log administrative sign-ins, privilege changes, integration updates, exports,

00:01:25.216 --> 00:01:26.449
and retention changes.

00:01:26.449 --> 00:01:29.739
Review unusual activity and protect the audit trail.

00:01:29.739 --> 00:01:33.851
Security controls should support authorized operations without enabling covert access,

00:01:33.851 --> 00:01:37.140
bypassing controls, or hiding actions from accountable oversight.
